      "observation": "The warning area initially shows a yellow strip and icon without a readable message. This is partial content at the bottom of Home.Upper's scroll viewport. The visible workstation section still says this startup has not been checked; continue/abandon controls and no-auto-processing caveat remain readable.",
      "sourceContext": "HomeView.xaml:207 defines Home.Upper with automatic vertical scrolling; lines236-252 place preset/recovery warnings outside the StartupDetails expander. HomeViewModel.cs:186-196 describes these as startup preset/recovery warnings; Strings.zh-CN.resx:1313 asks the operator to view workstation checks when startup preset validation failed. They are not simply hidden informational counts, but this review does not establish them as current live production blockers.",
      "expected": "When a startup warning exists, expose at least its meaningful warning summary in the compact initial view, or provide an equally clear visible indication directing the operator to its details.",
      "notEstablished": "Scrolling was not operated. No claim that the warning is inaccessible or that current production is permitted/blocked is made."
    }
